Track 3: Zenith Halo of the Dead-Mall
- Story & Context: Years after the mall was sealed by authorities, local urban explorers tell of the "Zenith Halo," a mysterious light anomaly that appears above the roof whenever a distant bell rings. The myth says that if you stand under the center of the rotunda, you can hear the faint, eternal rhythm of the Glass-Walkers still drumming in a loop that never ends. They say the music eventually claims you, turning you into just another flicker in the circuitry. "Light breaks the glass but leaves the sound" is the final, haunting message carved into the lobby's marble floor.
